# DVC 3 hashes RAW BYTES.
#
# DVC 2 normalised CRLF -> LF before hashing text files. DVC 3 removed that and
# treats every file as binary, so a CSV checked out on Windows with
# core.autocrlf=true gets a DIFFERENT md5 than the same file on macOS or Linux.
# In a mixed classroom that silently invalidates every .dvc pointer and every
# dvc.lock entry, and the symptom — "dvc status says modified but I changed
# nothing" — is painful to diagnose.
#
# Forcing LF makes the checkout byte-identical on every platform.
# See https://doc.dvc.org/user-guide/upgrade
#
# Belt and braces: the dataset generator also writes with lineterminator="\n",
# so the DVC-tracked file is LF regardless of how git checked out its inputs.
*.csv text eol=lf
